READING
  The mechanism `102` cites as guaranteeing answer-equivalence is the
  harness's byte-exact cross-variant comparison. For every region in
  the BEFORE set, the driver never called it, so it is not evidence
  about those regions in either direction. What remains as evidence
  there is the family's own unit tests, which is what the driver's own
  comment says: the variant crate's unit tests are 'the only fidelity
  check in the system'. For the answer-pinning families those tests
  exist, assert agreement against an independent oracle, and pass. For
  the regions listed above they do not exist.
